# IQM Lab website

A bilingual Jekyll site. Chinese pages live at `/`; English pages at `/en/`.
Both languages share the layouts and the data files, and every translatable
value is stored as a `zh:` / `en:` pair in one place. There is no automatic
translation or cross-language fallback: a missing key renders as blank, not as
the other language.

## Preview

Run `jekyll serve` from this directory and open http://localhost:4000.
Run `jekyll build` to generate `_site/`. Never edit `_site/` or `.jekyll-cache/`;
they are generated output. Restart the server after editing `_config.yml`.

## Where to edit

Both languages of each entry live in one shared data file:

| Content | Where |
| --- | --- |
| News, including the homepage panel | `_data/news.yml` |
| Member cards | `_data/member.yml` |
| Member activity album | `_data/album.yml` |
| Research cards and methods | `_data/research.yml` |
| Teaching cards and plans | `_data/teaching.yml` |
| Recruiting information | `_data/openings.yml` |

Page bodies are still one file per language:

| Content | Chinese | English |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Profile prose | `lingfang-lin.md` | `en/lingfang-lin.md` |
| Contact prose | `contact.md` | `en/contact.md` |
| Detailed news articles | `news/<slug>.md` | `news/en/<slug>.md` |
| Homepage introduction | `index.html` | `en/index.html` |

Publications are shared in `_data/publications.yml`; PDF files live in `pdfs/`.
Email and Google Scholar URL are shared in `_config.yml`.
Page titles, descriptions, headings, and introductions are in the YAML front
matter at the top of each page, so they are still written once per language.
Member-page recruiting callouts are there too.

In the data files, every translatable value is a two-key map:

```yaml
title:
  zh: 中文标题
  en: English title
```

Values that do not vary by language — `id`, `homepage`, `pin`, `photo`, the `methods`
list — stay plain scalars. Both languages of an item sit next to each other, so
they are edited in one place and cannot drift apart.

## Add news

Append an entry to the bottom of `_data/news.yml`:

```yaml
- id: new-publication-2026
  date: "2026-10-20"
  pin: false
  label:
    zh: 2026 · 论文发表
    en: 2026 · Publication
  title:
    zh: 我们的新论文
    en: Our new paper
  body:
    zh: 含 **粗体** 与 [论文链接](https://example.org) 的正文。
    en: Details with **bold text** and a [paper link](https://example.org).
  summary:
    zh: 可选的首页摘要。
    en: A short optional homepage summary.
  homepage: true
```

Items appear in reverse file order; append the newest at the bottom. Use a unique
`id` per item. The full news page shows all entries in this order.

The homepage panel considers only entries with `homepage: true`. Set `pin: true`
to keep an entry in the panel; `pin: false` or an omitted `pin` leaves it unpinned.
With fewer than five pinned entries, the panel fills the remaining slots with
the newest unpinned entries, up to five entries total. With five or more pinned
entries, it shows all pinned entries only. Selected entries always appear in
reverse file order; pinning affects inclusion, not display order.

`date` is shared by both languages. Use a quoted `YYYY-MM-DD` value such as
`date: "2026-10-20"`, or `date: ""` when the announcement date is unknown.
The full news page displays it at the top right of the card, opposite the
optional `label`; an empty or omitted date is hidden. The homepage keeps its
compact layout, showing `label` with `date` as a fallback when no label exists.
Dates do not affect display order.

`body` and `summary` support Markdown. If `summary` is
omitted, the homepage uses `body`. Set `homepage: false` to show an entry only on
the full news page. `SITE_EMAIL` in news text is replaced with the email from
`_config.yml`.

### Add a detailed news article

Optionally add `news-post` to a news entry. Its value is the article's filename
without `.md`, not its displayed title:

```yaml
  news-post: doctoral-student-award
```

Create `news/doctoral-student-award.md` with YAML front matter and Markdown:

```markdown
---
layout: news-post
lang: zh
title: 祝贺陈静妍荣获博士新生奖
description: 陈静妍荣获东南大学物理学院2026级博士新生奖。
nav_id: news
permalink: /news/doctoral-student-award.html
---

在这里撰写详细新闻内容，支持 **粗体**、链接和图片。

## 详情

更多新闻内容……
```

The Chinese news card gains a **查看详情** link only when the matching file exists
and has `lang: zh`. Entries without `news-post`, or referencing a missing file,
have no detail link. Homepage cards keep their compact summary format.

For an English translation, create `news/en/doctoral-student-award.md` with the
same filename, `layout: news-post`, `lang: en`, `nav_id: news`, English text and
metadata, and `permalink: /en/news/doctoral-student-award.html`. English cards
show **Read more** only when this English file exists; they never link to the
Chinese article as a fallback. All article source files stay inside `news/`.

The article layout uses `title` for its heading unless an optional `heading`
is provided; `intro` is also optional. It adds a localized link back to the news
listing. The language switch finds the matching article automatically, or links
to the other language's news listing if no translation exists. News articles
do not need `translation_path`. Use `relative_url` for local image/link URLs in
article content, for example `![合影]({{ '/assets/images/group-photo.webp' | relative_url }})`.

## Add a member

Copy an entry into `_data/member.yml`:

```yaml
- id: example-member
  name:
    zh: 示例成员
    en: Example Member
  role:
    zh: 博士生
    en: PhD student
  bio:
    zh: 研究方向与简短介绍。
    en: Research interests and a short introduction.
  photo: /assets/images/example.webp
  links:
  - url:
      zh: /example-member.html
      en: /en/example-member.html
    link_label:
      zh: 查看详情
      en: View profile
  - url: "mailto:example@example.org"
    link_label:
      zh: 邮箱
      en: Email
```

Upload the image to `assets/images/`. Cards appear in file order. `photo` and
`links` are optional. Add as many link entries as needed; links appear in list
order as separate clickable labels. `url` is a `zh:` / `en:` pair whenever the
target differs by language — a local path such as `/example-member.html` versus
`/en/example-member.html`. For `mailto:` and external URLs the same value simply
appears under both keys. `photo` is never translated. Names, roles, and
biographies are plain text.
For a longer profile, copy an existing `.md` profile, change its front matter
(including `permalink` and `translation_path`), and link to it from the member
entry. Create both language pages when using the shared language switch.
The member pages are `/member.html` and `/en/member.html`; old People URLs have
no redirects.

## Add member activity photos

The final card on both member pages is **组员活动相册 / Member Activities**.
Upload photos to `assets/images/activities/` (create the directory when adding
the first photo), then add entries to `_data/album.yml`:

```yaml
- image: /assets/images/activities/group-photo.webp
  subtitle:
    zh: 课题组合影
    en: Lab group photo
```

Replace the initial `[]` with your entries. Photos appear in file order. Each
entry requires `image` and both `subtitle.zh` and `subtitle.en`; subtitles are
plain text and also supply the image alt text. Images display in a 4:3 frame,
cropped to fit, so landscape photos work best.

Photos appear once in a horizontal row. Visitors can swipe, use a trackpad or
scrollbar, or focus the album and use the keyboard to scroll when photos exceed
the available width. CSS proximity snapping helps align photos after scrolling.
There is no automatic scrolling or pause/resume control. When all photos fit,
they stay stationary. An empty list shows a bilingual placeholder. The album
does not require JavaScript.

## Structure and layout changes

- `_layouts/default.html`: shared HTML document and background canvas.
- `_layouts/`: shared page templates for news, member, research, teaching,
  openings, publications, Markdown pages, and profiles.
- `_includes/`: shared navigation, head, footer, cards, and news components.
- `_data/navigation.yml`: navigation order, destinations, and bilingual labels.
- `_data/i18n.yml`: recurring interface labels and footer text, each written as
  a `zh:` / `en:` pair and read as `site.data.i18n.<key>[page.lang]`.
- `assets/style.scss`: appearance; `assets/ai-bg.js`: background animation.

Navigation links are shared in `_includes/navigation-links.html`. Above 980px,
the desktop links are always visible. At 980px and below, a native HTML
`details` / `summary` toggle opens the mobile menu; CSS switches the hamburger
and close icons and their localized labels. Navigation does not require
JavaScript. Use Enter or Space on the toggle to open or close it. The menu does
not close on Escape, and its open state persists when resizing between desktop
and mobile until toggled or a new page loads.

Pages have `lang`, `nav_id`, and `translation_path` in front matter (news
articles resolve their language-switch destination automatically, as above).
`translation_path` is the filename relative to the language root (empty for
home); it lets the language switch link to the matching page. `nav_id` matches
an ID in `_data/navigation.yml` and controls the active menu item.

Use spaces, not tabs, in YAML. Keep field names unchanged when editing text.
Templates read a data file as `site.data.<file>`, and each translatable field as
`item.<field>[page.lang]`. YAML rules that bite here:

- Write `zh:` / `en:` pairs in block style (two indented lines) rather than
  `{zh: …, en: …}` flow style; a comma inside the text breaks flow style.
- A value containing `: ` is a syntax error. A value containing ` #` is
  silently truncated at the `#`. Quote such text or use a `>-` block.
- Trailing spaces are stripped from unquoted values. `apply_text.en` in
  `_data/openings.yml` keeps its quotes because that trailing space is what
  separates the sentence from the email link.
- A missing `en:` or `zh:` key renders blank on that page and does not fail the
  build, so check both languages after editing.
